# Standard library errors on integers beyond what can be computed

```catala
declaration scope Errors:
  input case content integer
  output d content decimal
  output l content list of integer

scope Errors:
  definition d equals
    if case = 1 then Decimal.round_to_decimal of (1.0 / 3.0), 1000001
    else 0.0
  definition l equals
    if case = 2 then List.sequence of 0, 18446744073709551616 else []
```

A decimal without a finite expansion, rounded beyond 10^1000000:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Errors --input {"case":1} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: an integer is too large for this computation.
│
└─
#return code 123#
```

A list longer than a machine integer:

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope Errors --input {"case":2} --disable-warnings
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: an integer is too large for this computation.
│
└─
#return code 123#
```
